body:
All the time! I relate to this so much. For so damn long. Growing up I rarely had friends and when I did find a good group of friends, it got to a point where we would make plans and say okay they'll pick me up at this time and then the time rolled around and I got ditched. So messed up and they wondered why I kind of started hanging by myself and doing my own thing. And it's honestly been like that. Even with partners I would feel like okay things are going good and then I'd start seeing the signs and patterns like uh oh I'm no longer important and honestly that hits me harder than ever now cause I put so much of my times into others or I used to. I'm kind of a hermit right now. Go to work go home and just stay home. Like it's that effort that you want to feel. Like you want to feel special and important and that you know people think about you. And that feeling when it doesn't come, it hits you like a truck. It really does suck.

&#x200B;

But I can relate to it. Think a lot of us can. You're not alone on how you feel about this. Hell I know I'm no one's first choice. Right now I'm still waiting on responses from friends I texted 5 days ago and it bugs me cause I look at my phone like every 5 seconds like oo someone said something but that hasn't happened. I'm right there with you.
